[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62854,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Calcifying fibrous tumour (CFT) is a benign lesion composed of abundant hyalinized collagen, lymphoplasmacytic infiltration, and calcifications.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62855,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8817/0 Calcifying fibrous tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62856,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F74 &amp; XH7TH6 Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of peritoneum &amp; Calcifying fibrous tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62857,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> calcifying fibrous pseudotumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62858,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62859,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CFT usually occurs in the gastrointestinal tract, peritoneum, pleura, and mesentery {27196478; 12232572}, and it has been rarely reported in the ampulla of fallopian tube {24300534}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62860,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are typically identified incidentally but may cause symptoms related to an abdominal mass {28153506}. Patients with multiple tumours have been reported {27196478}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62861,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CFT seems to have a female predilection (M:F&nbsp;ratio: 0.79:1), most commonly in infants, young children, and young adults. The peritoneum is the fifth most common site of involvement, after the stomach, small intestine, pleura, and mesentery {27196478}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62862,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CFT may be related to trauma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62863,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>When CFT occurs at an early age, genetic predisposition has been suggested {27196478; 12817428}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62864,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most lesions are solitary, but they can be multiple. CFT appears as a well-defined, solid, and firm mass, with a mean size of 4.6&nbsp;cm and a wide size range {27196478}. The cut surface is tan-white and gritty.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62865,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is characterized by abundant, hypocellular, hyalinized collagen, with scattered calcifications that may be psammomatous, and a chronic lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate. It also contains scattered spindle cells with bland nuclei, fine chromatin, and inconspicuous nucleoli. Tumours are usually diffusely positive for factor&nbsp;XIIIa and CD34.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62866,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62867,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62868,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> abundant dense well-circumscribed hyalinized collagen with lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate, spindle cells, and psammomatous or dystrophic calcification.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62869,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62870,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 151,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CFT is benign and curable by local surgical resection, but a 10% recurrence rate has been reported {27196478}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:16:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]